,{"text":"Exercise conditioning"},{"text":"Patient education"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Respiratory Care Technology Degree","Clinical Internship","Respiratory Therapist","Clinical Respiratory Therapist","Senior Respiratory Therapist","ICU / Pulmonary / Pediatric Specialist","Respiratory Care Coordinator","Respiratory Care Manager","Clinical / Academic Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should aim for:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respiratory anatomy & physiology"},{"text":"Pulmonary pathology"},{"text":"Respiratory assessment"},{"text":"Oxygen therapy"},{"text":"ABG fundamentals"},{"text":"Pulmonary function testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Critical Care"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"CPAP/BiPAP"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Suctioning principles"},{"text":"Ventilator monitoring"},{"text":"Weaning principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical communication"},{"text":"Patient education"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Emergency response"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital patient monitoring"},{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Ventilator interfaces"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"AI-assisted healthcare technologies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"Respiratory Care graduate with strong knowledge of respiratory physiology and pulmonary disease, supervised clinical exposure to ICU and emergency respiratory care, competency in respiratory assessment and oxygen therapy, foundational mechanical-ventilation and airway-management skills, familiarity with pulmonary-function testing, and the ability to work effectively within multidisciplinary critical-care teams."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Respiratory Care Technology","Respiratory Assessment","Oxygen Therapy","Mechanical Ventilation","ICU Exposure","Pulmonary Diagnostics","Critical Care","Digital Monitoring"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strong specialized allied-health pathway, particularly for students interested in ICU, pulmonary medicine, emergency care, and technology-enabled critical care."},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"Keep “Respiratory Therapist” as the target career for this specialization. However, the database should distinguish it from Respiratory Therapy Technician/Technologist where institutions or employers use different qualification levels and job titles."}]}]}